Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: konaro-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         plasma-workspace (>= 4:6.3),
         plasma-desktop (>= 4:6.3),
         kde-style-breeze,
         kwin-style-breeze,
         breeze-cursor-theme,
         kf6-breeze-icon-theme,
         fonts-inter,
         systemd-zram-generator,
         mesa-utils
Recommends: konaro-glass, sddm, sddm-theme-breeze, plymouth, qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-controls
Description: Konaro OS desktop identity for KDE Plasma
 Default look and feel of Konaro OS on top of KDE Plasma 6:
  - global themes "Konaro Light" and "Konaro Dark" (neutral palette);
  - top bar (launcher, global menu, system tray, clock) and a floating,
    centered bottom dock;
  - welcome splash ("hello" in several languages, then "Welcome to Konaro");
  - wallpapers, color schemes, icons and SDDM/lock screen defaults.
 .
 Defaults are installed in /etc/xdg and apply to users that have not
 customized their own settings.

Package: konaro-lite
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, konaro-desktop (= ${source:Version}), systemd-zram-generator, mesa-utils
Description: Konaro OS Fênix Lite settings for older computers
 Makes Konaro lighter on old hardware (e.g. 2007 laptops with 2-3 GB of RAM)
 while keeping its look: compressed memory (zram), no glass/blur or wobbly
 effects, shorter animations, no background file indexing, a lighter Firefox,
 and automatic software rendering on graphics cards without OpenGL 2.
